    "cross-01": "Accept recovery procedures, behavioral tests and outcome checks as substantive evidence for their respective domains.",
    "cross-02": "Require coverage of both data-store isolation and independent identity-system controls. Treat role separation as supporting context rather than equivalent isolation.",
    "cross-03": "Require cross-domain evidence. Treat direct proxy-versus-outcome distinctions as substantive evidence and measured trade-offs as supporting context.",
    "cross-04": "Require both trade-offs for a complete answer. Keep the two mechanisms separate and treat metric-monitoring recommendations as supporting context.",
    "ai-03": "Cover both policy precedence and conflict resolution.",
    "ai-04": "Treat substantive automated answer release as the study's operational proxy rather than demonstrated downstream case closure.",
    "ai-07": "Include plausible alternative explanations to investigate, particularly changed human labeling practices.",
    "cy-01": "Distinguish employment-status approval from dataset-access approval; treat removal of old access as a related control.",
    "cy-04": "Distinguish scheduled expiry from actual revocation and require linked timing evidence to establish timely removal.",
    "econ-05": "A conceptual explanation is sufficient without requiring a numerical calculation.",
    "sw-02": "Treat separate legitimate actions and repeated delivery as essential distinctions.",
    "sw-05": "Focus on cross-store and corpus-state isolation rather than requiring every field of a complete production ranking cache key."
  },
